From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ir3: pass a4xx/a5xx SSBO accesses a byte offset again

Since SSBO intrinsics carry offset_shift, nir_lower_explicit_io folds the
dword shift into the offset source. lower_offset_for_ssbo copies that source
into the *_ssbo_ir3 intrinsic unchanged, but on a4xx/a5xx ldgb/stgb and the
SSBO atomics consume it as a byte address. Every 32-bit SSBO element i was
accessed at byte i instead of 4*i: stores overlapped and all data landed in
the first quarter of the buffer.

Shift the source back to bytes on those generations; a6xx and later only
use the shifted dword offset.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_lower_io_offsets.c
+++ b/src/freedreno/ir3/ir3_nir_lower_io_offsets.c
@@ -223,6 +223,15 @@
    int cur_shift = nir_intrinsic_offset_shift(intrinsic);
    int extra_shift = shift - cur_shift;

+   /* a4xx/a5xx ldgb/stgb/atomics also take the original offset source, as a
+    * byte address, so undo the offset_shift that nir_lower_explicit_io
+    * folded into it.
+    */
+   if (c->gen < 6 && cur_shift > 0) {
+      new_intrinsic->src[offset_src_idx] = nir_src_for_ssa(
+         nir_ishl_imm(b, intrinsic->src[offset_src_idx].ssa, cur_shift));
+   }
+
    /* TODO if the intrinsic has a BASE, we have to be careful when inserting a
     * right shift as the offset may be negative. So we'd have to add the BASE to
     * the offset before shifting. For now, as our input intrinsics don't support
